            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='2' />
            <_.fcp.DashboardRoundedCorners.true...format attr='corner-radius' value='12' />
            <format attr='background-color' value='#171a20' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='13000' id='43' type-v2='empty' w='98571' x='714' y='7600'>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#212f38' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='2' />
            <_.fcp.DashboardRoundedCorners.true...format attr='corner-radius' value='12' />
            <format attr='background-color' value='#171a20' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='3600' id='3' name='KPI Winners' show-title='false' w='22857' x='1429' y='3200' />
        <zone h='3600' id='5' name='KPI Chance' show-title='false' w='22857' x='25714' y='3200' />
        <zone h='3600' id='8' name='KPI Pole' show-title='false' w='22857' x='50000' y='3200' />
        <zone h='3600' id='9' name='KPI Races' show-title='false' w='22857' x='74286' y='3200' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1000' id='12' type-v2='text' w='78929' x='19643' y='600'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='36'>How much does Saturday tell us about Sunday?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1940' id='13' type-v2='text' w='78929' x='19643' y='1800'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='14' italic='true'>Qualifying sets the starting grid, but the car already tells us a lot about who will win. This asks how much extra Saturday adds, using 329 races from 2010 to 2025. Knowing only team and driver form, about six drivers are realistic contenders. Add the grid and it narrows to about four. It is a prediction result, not a claim that pole causes wins.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='3500' id='18' is-scaled='1' param='Image/formula-1-seeklogo.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='14286' x='1429' y='0' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='900' id='25' type-v2='text' w='52643' x='1429' y='7800'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='24'>How often does the driver on pole actually win?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='7600' id='26' name='Pole Ring' show-title='false' w='27143' x='1429' y='10600' />
        <zone h='9600' id='31' name='Pole By Year' show-title='false' w='60714' x='30714' y='8800' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1660' id='32' type-v2='text' w='97143' x='1429' y='18700'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='14' italic='true'>The driver on grid slot 1 won 172 of 329 races (52%), so pole is worth a lot, but it is far from a guarantee. The bars show how that rate moved season by season, from a low of 38% in 2019 to a high of 67% in 2025. The dashed line is the overall average. With only 16 to 24 races a year, a swing of 10 points either way is within what luck alone can produce, so individual seasons should not be over-read. This number is also flattering to Saturday, because the fastest car tends to take pole in the first place. The next section shows how much of it the car explains.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='900' id='35' type-v2='text' w='64000' x='1429' y='21200'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>How often would we expect them to win before qualifying?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='10400' id='36' name='Gap Dumbbell Lines' show-title='false' w='97143' x='1429' y='22500' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1600' id='37' type-v2='text' w='97143' x='1429' y='33200'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='14' italic='true' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Before the grid is known, the car and driver alone gave the pole-sitter about a 22% chance of winning (grey). They actually won 53% of the time (red), so qualifying adds about 31 points on top of what the car already told us. The gap is smallest in 2019, at about 17 points, and largest in 2025, at about 52. The red dots skip three races with nobody on grid slot 1, so they sit slightly above the 52% in the section above. This gap is what Saturday adds. The car alone gets a long way towards pole&apos;s success, but qualifying still tells us far more than the car&apos;s form.</run>
            <run lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='14000' id='49' type-v2='empty' w='98571' x='714' y='35400'>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#2a2f38' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
            <_.fcp.DashboardRoundedCorners.true...format attr='corner-radius' value='12' />
            <format attr='background-color' value='#171a20' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='900' id='50' type-v2='text' w='73786' x='1429' y='35800'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='24'>How quickly does the win chance fall as drivers start further back?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='10000' id='51' name='Grid Staircase' show-title='false' w='97143' x='1429' y='37000' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='2000' id='52' type-v2='text' w='97143' x='1429' y='47200'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='14' italic='true'>Red bars show how often the driver starting from each grid slot actually won: about 53% from slot 1, 26% from slot 2 and 11% from slot 3, then rare from slot 4 back. The grey line is what the car-and-driver baseline expected from each slot without knowing the grid. At the front it is too cautious (22% for slot 1 and 17% for slot 2, against 53% and 26% in reality). For slots 4 to 6 it expects two to four times more wins than really happened, because it cannot see how much a poor start costs. Slot 1 reads 53% here, not 52%, because three races had nobody on that slot and are left out. From slot 7 back, each slot has only a few wins in total, so small bumps such as slot 10 are noise.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='3300' id='59' name='Callout Gap' show-title='false' w='19286' x='78929' y='21400' />
        <zone h='4400' id='62' name='Callout Slots' show-title='false' w='23571' x='75000' y='37040' />
        <zone h='13000' id='67' type-v2='empty' w='98571' x='714' y='50000'>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#2a2f38' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
            <_.fcp.DashboardRoundedCorners.true...format attr='corner-radius' value='12' />
            <format attr='background-color' value='#171a20' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='900' id='68' type-v2='text' w='59643' x='1429' y='50400'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='24'>Does Saturday only matter when one car is dominant?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='8400' id='69' name='Season Slope' show-title='false' w='53571' x='1429' y='52000' />
        <zone h='8400' id='70' name='Callout Drop' show-title='false' w='33571' x='60714' y='52000' />
        <zone h='2000' id='71' type-v2='text' w='97143' x='1429' y='60700'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='14' italic='true'>Plausible winners is how many drivers the model treats as realistic contenders in a race. In close seasons, the car and driver alone leave about 7 (red, 169 races), and the grid narrows that to about 4. In runaway seasons, where one team wins most races, the car already narrows it to about 4.7, and the grid trims it to 3.3 (grey, 160 races). So Saturday matters in both, and more when there is no obvious favourite. The 16 seasons are split at the median share of races won by the top team, so 2011 and 2013 sit right on the line. Part of the bigger drop in close seasons is simply that the car alone says less there, so there is more for the grid to add.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='13000' id='74' type-v2='empty' w='98571' x='714' y='63400'>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#2a2f38' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
            <_.fcp.DashboardRoundedCorners.true...format attr='corner-radius' value='12' />
            <format attr='background-color' value='#171a20' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='8400' id='75' name='Circuit Card' show-title='false' w='33571' x='60714' y='65000' />
        <zone h='8400' id='76' name='Circuit Map' show-title='false' w='50000' x='1429' y='65000' />
        <zone h='900' id='79' type-v2='text' w='62857' x='1429' y='63900'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='24'>Does Saturday matter more at some tracks than others?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='2000' id='80' type-v2='text' w='97143' x='1429' y='74000'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='14' italic='true'>Each dot is a circuit, sized by how many races we have there and coloured by how much the starting grid improved our prediction: red for a big improvement, grey for little or none. Click a circuit to see its numbers on the right, and click it again to go back to all circuits. Among circuits with at least 8 races, Monaco stands out (+1.02) and Sochi is the lowest (-0.20), which fits the idea that grid position matters most where overtaking is hard. The greyest dot is Miami (-1.15), where the grid made predictions worse, but that rests on only four races, so it is noise. Overall the pattern is not reliable: shuffling the circuit labels at random gives a spread this large about 42% of the time, so the map is for exploring and not a verdict.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='1520' id='81' name='Circuit Map' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.1wdm7i91w5j1k214jgw2p1celige].[avg:gain:qk]' type-v2='color' w='10000' x='41143' y='65020' />
      </zones>
