                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#e6e6e6' fontname='Helvetica' fontsize='14' italic='true'>The driver on grid slot 1 won 172 of 329 races (52%), so pole is worth a lot, but it is far from a guarantee. The bars show how that rate moved season by season, from a low of 38% in 2019 to a high of 67% in 2025. The dashed line is the overall average. With only 16 to 24 races a year, a swing of 10 points either way is within what luck alone can produce, so individual seasons should not be over-read. This number is also flattering to Saturday, because the fastest car tends to take pole in the first place. The next section shows how much of it the car explains.</run>
